# Recursion and mutual recursion keep their frames: a jump onto a function's entry point
# is a call even when the function is active, and a jump landing on the return address
# read off the stack at the call is its return. No node: the contract is compiled here
# and run on a local chain.
# REQUIRES: soldb
# RUN: %soldb compile %S/../examples/Recursion.sol -o %t.out --solc %{solc_path} > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: printf 'break fact\ncontinue\ncontinue\ncontinue\nbt\nfinish\nbt\nfinish\nbt\nquit\n' | %soldb run %t.out/Recursion.bin "fact(uint256)" 3 --ethdebug-dir 0x5FbDB2315678afecB367f032d93F642f64180aa3:Recursion:%t.out -i 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=FACT %s

# FACT: Breakpoint #1 set at function Recursion.fact at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:6
# FACT: Breakpoint #1 hit at step {{[0-9]+}}, function Recursion.fact
# FACT: Breakpoint #1 hit at step {{[0-9]+}}, function Recursion.fact
# FACT: Breakpoint #1 hit at step {{[0-9]+}}, function Recursion.fact
# Three activations of fact, each at the call site of the next, each with the argument
# it was entered with: this trace's calldata proved where the compiler leaves them.
# FACT: #0  fact(n = 1) at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:6
# FACT-NEXT: #1  fact(n = 2) at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:10
# FACT-NEXT: #2  fact(n = 3) at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:10
# FACT-NEXT: #3  Recursion at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:5
# `finish` returns one activation at a time, not out of the whole recursion.
# FACT: #0  fact(n = 2) at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:10
# FACT-NEXT: #1  fact(n = 3) at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:10
# FACT-NEXT: #2  Recursion at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:5
# FACT: #0  fact(n = 3) at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:10
# FACT-NEXT: #1  Recursion at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:5

# RUN: printf 'break ping\ncontinue\ncontinue\nbt\nfinish\nbt\nquit\n' | %soldb run %t.out/Recursion.bin "ping(uint256)" 2 --ethdebug-dir 0x5FbDB2315678afecB367f032d93F642f64180aa3:Recursion:%t.out -i 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=PING %s

# PING: Breakpoint #1 hit at step {{[0-9]+}}, function Recursion.ping
# PING: Breakpoint #1 hit at step {{[0-9]+}}, function Recursion.ping
# PING: #0  ping(n = 0) at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:13
# PING-NEXT: #1  pong(n = 1) at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:24
# PING-NEXT: #2  ping(n = 2) at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:17
# PING-NEXT: #3  Recursion at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:5
# PING: #0  pong(n = 1) at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:24
# PING-NEXT: #1  ping(n = 2) at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:17
# PING-NEXT: #2  Recursion at {{.*}}Recursion.sol:5
